---
import * as stylex from "@stylexjs/stylex";
import { styles as shared } from "../styles/shared.stylex";
import { styles } from "./installNote.stylex";
---

<div {...stylex.attrs(styles.card, shared.above)}>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 160 148"
    aria-hidden="true"
    {...stylex.attrs(styles.hazard)}
  >
    <use href="#s-hazard" />
  </svg>

  <p {...stylex.attrs(styles.kicker)}>heads up before you install</p>
  <h3 {...stylex.attrs(styles.title)}>
    macOS will say it cannot verify the app
  </h3>
  <p {...stylex.attrs(styles.body)}>
    This build is signed but not notarized, because notarization needs the
    $99/year Apple Developer Program and this is a hobby project. So the first
    launch gets a Gatekeeper warning. That is expected. Here is the way through
    it:
  </p>
  <div {...stylex.attrs(styles.flows)}>
    <div>
      <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.flowLabel)}>macOS 15 or later</span>
      <p {...stylex.attrs(styles.flow)}>
        Open the app. When macOS says it cannot be verified, choose Done. Then
        open System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security, find the AngryKeyboard
        message, and click Open Anyway.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span {...stylex.attrs(styles.flowLabel)}>macOS 14</span>
      <p {...stylex.attrs(styles.flow)}>
        Control-click the app and choose Open.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p {...stylex.attrs(styles.foot)}>
    After that it asks for Input Monitoring, which it needs to hear your keys.
    It only listens.
  </p>
</div>
